  "reasoning": "Extensive scientific research and clinical evaluations have repeatedly failed to find a causal link between MSG (monosodium glutamate) and symptoms like headaches or numbness, collectively termed \"Chinese restaurant syndrome.\" Major health and regulatory authorities, including the U.S. FDA, the World Health Organization (WHO), and the European Food Safety Authority, consider MSG \"generally recognized as safe\" (GRAS) at typical dietary levels. Double-blind, placebo-controlled studies have demonstrated that self-identified sensitive individuals do not reliably react to MSG when given with food.",
